  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A conducting ring is placed in a magnetic field. There is a current in the coil so that the direction of electron flow in the coil is anti-clockwise. As a result of the current in the coil and the magnetic field, an electromagnetic force acts on the coil upwards.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>What is the direction of the magnetic field?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\">Upwards</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\">Downwards</li>\n<li data-label=\"C\">Into the page</li>\n<li data-label=\"D\">Out of the page</li>\n</ol>"
  },
